# Git Branching

The Project orchestrator owns the Ledger and assigns task IDs. Workers and humans never invent an ID.

Task ID: `<PREFIX>-<n>` matching `^[A-Z][A-Z0-9]{1,9}-[1-9][0-9]*$` (example `IDE-42`). The prefix is per repo.

There are only two long-lived branches: `development` (integration) and `main` (live).

| Branch | Who | Role |
|---|---|---|
| `development` | integration | Pull requests from `issue/*`, `phase/*`, and `dev/*` |
| `main` | protected | Pull requests only from `promote/main/*` |
| `issue/<PREFIX>-<n>-<slug>` | worker | Cut from latest `origin/development`. Slug is lowercase `[a-z0-9-]`, max 48 characters |
| `phase/<...>` | orchestrator | Package branch |
| `dev/<...>` | human | Rare ad-hoc IDE work |
| `promote/main/<...>` | orchestrator | Temporary branch cut from a `development` commit |

One GitHub Issue per Phase (readable summary). No GitHub Issue per branch or task.

## Flow

`issue/*` → PR to `development` (orchestrator) → green Full CI + independent review → merge → `promote/main/*` → `main`

Workers push their branch and never open pull requests.

## Session entry

- New session with a Ledger ID: `agentsetup` runs `python3 scripts/gitops/create_issue_branch.py --id <PREFIX>-<n> --slug <slug>`
- No ID: stop and ask the Project orchestrator
- Already open on the wrong branch: `agentcomply`
